https://github.com/ekuefler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-11-21T22:43:33Z","updated_at":"2015-11-21T22:43:33Z","body":"Huh OK, looks like it more subtle than I thought. I tried a fresh repo with a hand-built jar and it was able to extract it alright. There's also an interaction with sandboxing - if I pass `--genrule_strategy=standalone`, I don't get the permission error. Unfortunately this means I can't tell how much it's creating before it dies since I can't tell what happened in the sandbox after the fact. web.xml permissions are 644.\n\nI trimmed my rules down a bit, here's what I have now:\n\n```\nfilegroup(\n  name = \"backend-webinf\",\n  srcs = [\n    \"webapp/backend/appengine-web.xml\",\n    \"webapp/backend/logging.properties\",\n    \"webapp/backend/web.xml\",\n  ],\n)\ngenrule(\n  name = \"backend\",\n  srcs = [\n    \":backend-webinf\",\n  ],\n  outs = [\n    \"backend.war\",\n  ],\n  tools = [\n    \"//third_party/ijar:zipper\",\n  ],\n  cmd = \"\"\"\n    mkdir -p war/WEB-INF\n    cd war\n\n    for file in $(locations :backend-webinf); do\n      cp ../$$file WEB-INF\n    done\n    ls -la WEB-INF\n\n    ../$(location //third_party/ijar:zipper) Cc ../$@ $$(find . -type f | cut -c 3-)\n\"\"\",\n\n)\ngenrule(\n  name = \"server\",\n  srcs = [\n    \":backend\",\n  ],\n  outs = [\n    \"server.ear\"\n  ],\n  tools = [\n    \"//third_party/ijar:zipper\",\n  ],\n  cmd = \"\"\"\n    pwd\n    echo $(location :backend)\n    $(location //third_party/ijar:zipper) x $(location :backend)\n    echo \"success\"\n\"\"\",\n)\n```\n\nHere's the output I get from building the server target:\n\n```\n# bazel build src/main/java/com/ekuefler/server\nINFO: Found 1 target...\nINFO: From Executing genrule //src/main/java/com/ekuefler/server:backend:\ntotal 24\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 21 22:32 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 21 22:32 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 nobody nogroup  432 Nov 21 22:32 appengine-web.xml\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 21 22:32 lib\n-rw-r--r-- 1 nobody nogroup   14 Nov 21 22:32 logging.properties\n-rw-r--r-- 1 nobody nogroup 2110 Nov 21 22:32 web.xml\nINFO: From Executing genrule //src/main/java/com/ekuefler/server:server:\n/root/.cache/bazel/_bazel_root/c9fadd9098376b2dddd3da4175fdad4b/master\nbazel-out/local_linux-fastbuild/genfiles/src/main/java/com/ekuefler/server/backend.war\nCannot open file /root/.cache/bazel/_bazel_root/c9fadd9098376b2dddd3da4175fdad4b/master/WEB-INF/web.xml for writing: Permission denied\n/bin/bash: line 3:  2665 Aborted                 (core dumped) bazel-out/local_linux-fastbuild/bin/third_party/ijar/zipper x bazel-out/local_linux-fastbuild/genfiles/src/main/java/com/ekuefler/server/backend.war\nERROR: /master/src/main/java/com/ekuefler/server/BUILD:119:1: Executing genrule //src/main/java/com/ekuefler/server:server failed: bash failed: error executing command /bin/bash -c ... (remaining 1 argument(s) skipped).\nTarget //src/main/java/com/ekuefler/server:server failed to build\nUse --verbose_failures to see the command lines of failed build steps.\nINFO: Elapsed time: 0.531s, Critical Path: 0.18s\n```\n\nFile permissions before creating the backend war look ok according to ls, and the echoed paths look fine up until when ijar zipper is invoked. Again it works okay if I disable sandboxing, so maybe the root cause has something to do with that. If nothing jumps out at you from this I can keep trying to trim this down to a minimal repro that I can share, but it will take a bit more work.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/158688429/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ekuefler","id":666477,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NjQ3Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/666477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler","html_url":"https://github.com/ekuefler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ekuefler/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/159562845","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/630#issuecomment-159562845","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/630","id":159562845,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE1OTU2Mjg0NQ==","user":{"login":"damienmg","id":3721087,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjEwODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3721087?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/damienmg","html_url":"https://github.com/damienmg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/us