git@github.com:bazelbuild/bazel.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel","homepage":"https://bazel.build","size":992874,"stargazers_count":24886,"watchers_count":24886,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4359,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1819,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["bazel","build","build-system","correct","fast","multi-language","scalable","test"],"visibility":"public","forks":4359,"open_issues":1819,"watchers":24886,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"This issue looks very similar to #630, in a slightly different context.\n\nI'm using ijar zipper to extract a war that contains entries for files, but not for the directories containing those files. This works on my Linux machine whether running in sandbox or standalone. It fails on a coworker's Macbook. When passing \"xv\" to the zipper to get verbose output, we see output like this on OSX:\n\n```\n/Users/[path]/BUILD:3:1: Executing genrule //[path]/editor:editor failed: bash failed: error executing command /bin/bash -c ... (remaining 1 argument(s) skipped): com.google.devtools.build.lib.shell.AbnormalTerminationException: Process terminated by signal 6.\nf 644 BUILD\nf 644 editor/Images/Dev/gameboard_blank.png\nCannot create folder /private/var/tmp/_bazel_root/c435e5cceb9c31b5a6ba1d5afff082fd/Master/war/editor/Images: Permission denied\n/bin/bash: line 6: 19908 Abort trap: 6           ../external/bazel_tools/tools/zip/zipper/zipper xv ../$file\n```\n\nInspecting the filesystem afterwards, we see that `.../Master/war`, which is created by the genrule, has the correct 755 permissions. However, `.../Master/war/editor`, which should have been created implicitly by the zipper, only has 644 permissions. So the zipper dies when it tries to create `Images` inside of `editor`.\n\nWe're on Bazel 0.3.1 but the issue appears to be present in earlier versions. Again, this looks OSX specific, building the same target works fine on Linux.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/1601/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/1601/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]